       :verbatim
       "\nTwo bounds, stated here because they are easier to hold in a paper than in a\nmeeting. First, the honest claim is \\emph{diagnostic, not evolutionary}: that\nan organisation instrumented this way will be shown where its decisions are\ncoupled and where they are not, and \\emph{not} that instrumenting it causes\nimprovement. The selective half of the argument is a plan with criteria fixed\nin advance and nothing yet measured; a pitch implying otherwise is claiming an\nunrun experiment.\n\nSecond, the first engagement is not a validated diagnostic being applied. It is\n\\textbf{the instrument being built on a real subject}, and it should be scoped\nand priced as construction. This is not a hedge --- it is the same claim this\npaper makes about itself, applied to the first client rather than to the first\noperator."}]},
